'''FX-6'''<ref name="The Dark Side" /> was an [[FX-9 surgical assistant]]<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> that built [[Grievous]] after the [[Kaleesh]]<ref name="The Dark Side" /> was involved in a gruesome [[shuttle]] crash that almost [[Death|killed]] him<ref name="Galaxy at War">''[[Star Wars: A Galaxy at War]]''</ref> and destroyed most of his original body.<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref>

In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], including FX-6's appearance on [[Coruscant]], to [[19 BBY]].</ref> FX-6 was present at the [[Grand Republic Medical Facility]] on [[Coruscant]] with a [[DD-13 medical assistant droid]], [[2-1B surgical droid]],<ref name="The Dark Side" /> and another [[FX-9 surgical assistant]].<ref name="Journeys Beginnings">''[[Star Wars Journeys: Beginnings]]''</ref> and performed [[blood]] transfusions during the reconstruction of [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]]<ref name="Character Encyclopedia" /> following his [[Duel on Mustafar|defeat]] at the hands of [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] on [[Mustafar]].<ref name="Episode III" /> At some point after [[12 BBY]],<ref name="Fortress Vader date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' states that [[Fortress Vader]] was completed forty-six [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|Starkiller Incident]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[34 ABY]]. Therefore, the [[fortress]] was constructed in [[12 BBY]].</ref> FX-6, and the DD-13 and 2-1B [[medical droid]]s, were moved to Vader's [[Fortress Vader|fortress]] on Mustafar, where they continued to design and implement improvements to [[Darth Vader's armor|Vader's armor]] under his supervision.<ref name="The Dark Side" />

